{
  // Type-checks the package INCLUDING its out-of-src tests.
  //
  // Extends the BASE config rather than ./tsconfig.json on purpose: that one carries `rootDir: "src"` +
  // `outDir` for the dist build, and a rootDir cannot contain files outside itself. Inheriting it yields
  // hundreds of TS6059s — first for test/, then for the cross-package `../../core/src` imports the itests use
  // deliberately (bun's per-package node_modules means a relative barrel import is the working shape there).
  // Emit settings are irrelevant here; this config only ever runs with noEmit.
  //
  // Why it exists: the itests were never type-checked at all. `bun test` compiles them at run time, so a
  // wrong signature — applyMigrations takes a connection string, not an options object — passed typecheck,
  // passed lint, and failed in CI behind a misleading "password authentication failed for user runner".
  //
  // There is NO exclude list. It started as a 17-file / 56-error ratchet and is now empty: every test file in
  // the package is checked. Keep it that way — an exclusion here is a file nobody type-checks, which is the
  // exact condition that let the bug above through.
  //
  // The bulk of those 56 were one shape: `const [r] = await sql...` then `r.foo`, asserting "this returned a
  // row" without saying so. They are fixed, not silenced — `one()` in itestDb.ts states it and fails with the
  // expected shape, and where a test had ALREADY asserted non-emptiness on the line above, optional chaining
  // says so to the compiler without changing what the assertion catches.
  //
  // One was not a type problem at all: masterBackfill captured `personsBeforeRun1` and never compared it —
  // an assertion someone meant to write. It is written now (the no-junk-mint property), because deleting the
  // variable would have erased the evidence that something was missing.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": { "noEmit": true },
  "include": ["src", "test"]
}
